00:37:00.260 --> 00:37:04.940
freezing those settings so it's kind of
a more subtle effect than your normal

00:37:04.940 --> 00:37:11.930
chemotherapy and so when we think about
cancer the idea is that the sort of a

00:37:11.930 --> 00:37:16.069
big-picture view the idea is that you
have tumor suppressor genes and then you

00:37:16.069 --> 00:37:20.390
have oncogenes and so the tumor
suppressor genes help suppress the tumor

00:37:20.390 --> 00:37:24.470
growth and then the oncogenes promote
the tumor growth and then in a healthy

00:37:24.470 --> 00:37:28.369
individual you always have this balance
so we all have tumor suppressor genes

00:37:28.369 --> 00:37:31.730
and we all have oncogenes but there's
always got to be a balance between the

00:37:31.730 --> 00:37:36.880
two and then when things go out of
balance that's when you can get cancer

00:37:36.880 --> 00:37:43.250
and so we can go back to our ski trail
metaphor and like I was saying before

00:37:43.250 --> 00:37:50.630
that when you start a cell from sort of
an embryo state it has to divide and

00:37:50.630 --> 00:37:55.190
differentiate and then it can turn into
a blood cell or a brain cell or an

00:37:55.190 --> 00:37:59.000
immune cell or a heart cell well in
addition it could also turn into a tumor

00:37:59.000 --> 00:38:02.900
cell as well and so it's important to
understand you know how this process

00:38:02.900 --> 00:38:09.680
worked and how epigenetics control
the change of these cells and so ideally

00:38:09.680 --> 00:38:15.680
what the the goal here is to start with
a cancer cell and then reprogram it so

00:38:15.680 --> 00:38:20.390
wipe out all its epigenetic marks and
take it to the top of the hill and then

00:38:20.390 --> 00:38:25.580
let it be programmed into a cell that
can actually be beneficial to your body

00:38:25.580 --> 00:38:33.710
rather than taking it away from you and
so as far as the epigenetics goes in in

00:38:33.710 --> 00:38:37.850
just normal cells as I was saying before
you can imagine it as these you know

00:38:37.850 --> 00:38:41.810
thousands of these plastic spools
hovering in in the auditorium and

00:38:41.810 --> 00:38:45.950
turning things on and off and so forth
well it's going to turn the tumor

00:38:45.950 --> 00:38:50.600
suppressor genes on and you're going to
have your uncle genes turned off and

00:38:50.600 --> 00:38:53.930
then in addition there's sort of a third
class of genes that are important for

00:38:53.930 --> 00:38:59.330
cancer and these I just call sort of DNA
chaos genes where they could cause kind

00:38:59.330 --> 00:39:04.910
of swapping of different parts of genes
from from one spot to another and in

00:39:04.910 --> 00:39:10.700
those case you also want those turned
off in a normal cell but in in cancer

00:39:10.700 --> 00:39:14.570
cells what happens is that the tumor
suppressors the things that are supposed

00:39:14.570 --> 00:39:20.390
to suppress the tumors are actually off
resulting in in tumor growth and then

00:39:20.390 --> 00:39:24.740
the oncogenes are turned on also
resulting in tumor growth and then there

00:39:24.740 --> 00:39:29.480
are also other kinds of situations where
these so called DNA chaos genes are also

00:39:29.480 --> 00:39:33.920
